2026-10-29 07:39:21 [kimi-k3.1-pro] 🟠nitrologic Relay 2.0.6 kimi-k3.1-pro 🜁 🪠 🧊 $0.008 508B 28.61s
2026-10-29 07:39:21 [kimi-k3.1-pro] Yes—using built-in Find and Replace:
2026-10-29 07:39:21 [kimi-k3.1-pro] 
2026-10-29 07:39:21 [kimi-k3.1-pro] 1. Open Replace with `Ctrl+H` (`Cmd+Option+F` on macOS).
2026-10-29 07:39:21 [kimi-k3.1-pro] 2. Enable Use Regular Expression (the `.*` button).
2026-10-29 07:39:21 [kimi-k3.1-pro] 3. In Find, enter:
2026-10-29 07:39:21 [kimi-k3.1-pro]    `^\s*\n`
2026-10-29 07:39:21 [kimi-k3.1-pro] 4. Leave Replace empty.
2026-10-29 07:39:21 [kimi-k3.1-pro] 5. Click Replace All.
2026-10-29 07:39:21 [kimi-k3.1-pro] 
2026-10-29 07:39:21 [kimi-k3.1-pro] This removes empty lines and lines containing only whitespace. To remove only completely empty
2026-10-29 07:39:21 [kimi-k3.1-pro] lines, use `^\r?\n` instead.
